warning[SCXML038]: ecmascript syntax error in `cond`: the expression ends before it is complete
 --> tests/ui/scxml038-ecmascript-parse-paths.scx:4:38
  |
4 |     <transition event="e1" cond="x ? 1" target="b"/>
  |                                  ----- while parsing this `cond`
  |                                      ^ syntax error
  |
  = note: a condition that cannot be parsed raises `error.execution` and evaluates as false, so this condition can never hold
  = help: a `?` conditional needs both branches: `test ? whenTrue : whenFalse`
  = spec: SCXML 1.0 §5.9 Expressions
  = spec: SCXML 1.0 §B.2 The ECMAScript Data Model

warning[SCXML038]: ecmascript syntax error in `cond`: the left side of `=` cannot be assigned to
 --> tests/ui/scxml038-ecmascript-parse-paths.scx:5:40
  |
5 |     <transition event="e2" cond="x + 1 = 2" target="b"/>
  |                                  --------- while parsing this `cond`
  |                                        ^ not assignable
  |
  = note: a condition that cannot be parsed raises `error.execution` and evaluates as false, so this condition can never hold
  = help: `=` assigns, and only a variable or a property such as `a.b` or `a[0]` can be assigned; to compare, write `===` (or `==`)
  = spec: SCXML 1.0 §5.9 Expressions
  = spec: SCXML 1.0 §B.2 The ECMAScript Data Model
help: compare with `===`
  |
5 |     <transition event="e2" cond="x + 1 === 2" target="b"/>
  |                                        ~~~

warning[SCXML076]: `cond` on `<transition>` has a side effect
 --> tests/ui/scxml038-ecmascript-parse-paths.scx:6:40
  |
6 |     <transition event="e3" cond="o.a.b = 3" target="b"/>
  |                                        ^ `=` assigns `o.a.b` instead of comparing it
  |
  = note: SCXML 1.0 §5.9.1: "Conditional expressions in conformant SCXML documents SHOULD NOT have side effects." (Appendix B's "This language MUST not have side effects" contradicts official IRP test 444, `cond="++var1==2"`; see docs/spec-errata.md)
  = help: to compare, use `===` (or `==`); to change the value, move the assignment into `<assign>` in the transition
  = spec: SCXML 1.0 Appendix B Data Models
  = spec: SCXML 1.0 §5.9.1 Conditional Expressions
  = spec: SCXML 1.0 §B.2 The ECMAScript Data Model
help: compare with `===`
  |
6 |     <transition event="e3" cond="o.a.b === 3" target="b"/>
  |                                        ~~~

