warning[SCXML038]: ecmascript syntax error in `cond`: `let` declares a variable, which a `cond` cannot do
 --> tests/ui/scxml038-ecmascript-parse-paths.scx:8:34
  |
8 |     <transition event="e5" cond="let y = 1" target="b"/>
  |                                  ^^^ a declaration, not an expression
  |                                  --------- while parsing this `cond`
  |
  = note: a condition that cannot be parsed raises `error.execution` and evaluates as false, so this condition can never hold
  = help: a `cond` must be an expression: declare the variable with `<data id="y" expr="…"/>` in the `<datamodel>`, or set it with `<assign location="y" expr="…"/>`
  = spec: SCXML 1.0 §5.9 Expressions
  = spec: SCXML 1.0 §B.2 The ECMAScript Data Model

